INSERT INTO `irb_application_mitigation_strategy` VALUES (1,1,1,NULL,1),(2,3,1,NULL,1),(3,6,1,'paredness for Epi-Zoonotic emergencies in six Eastern Africa countries',1),(4,1,2,NULL,1),(5,3,2,NULL,1),(6,6,2,'Situational analysis of preparedness for Epi-Zoonotic emergencies in six Eastern Africa countries',1),(7,1,3,NULL,1),(8,5,3,NULL,1),(9,6,3,'x Eastern Africa countries',1),(10,1,4,NULL,1),(11,5,4,NULL,1),(12,6,4,'dsaasd',1),(13,1,7,NULL,1),(14,3,7,NULL,1),(15,6,7,'Aerosol-generating procedures',1),(16,1,8,NULL,1),(17,5,8,NULL,1),(18,6,8,'pecial/vulnerable populatio',1),(19,2,9,NULL,1),(20,5,9,NULL,1),(21,6,9,'none',1),(22,1,10,NULL,1),(23,4,10,NULL,1),(24,6,10,'Test with Asdenikachew',1),(25,1,11,NULL,1),(26,3,11,NULL,1),(27,6,11,'xxxxxxxx',1),(28,2,12,'The study design (prospective cohort), qualitative approach, and follow-up enforced us to make face-to-face data collection.',1),(29,5,12,NULL,1),(30,6,12,'All data collectors and supervisors should use all prevention methods of COVID-19 like  wearing the mask, using hand sanitizer, keeping distance, and informing similar to study subjects.',1),(31,1,13,NULL,1),(32,2,13,NULL,1),(33,3,13,NULL,1),(34,4,13,NULL,1),(35,5,13,NULL,1),(36,6,13,'All data collectors ,supervisors and the students first will be aware to protect them self and other from Covid 19.The precautions will be applied by wearing masks,using sanitizer and decreasing suffocation.',1),(47,1,16,NULL,1),(48,2,16,NULL,1),(49,3,16,NULL,1),(50,4,16,NULL,1),(51,5,16,NULL,1),(52,6,16,'Not applicable to systematic reviews and meta-analysis',1),(53,1,17,NULL,1),(54,2,17,NULL,1),(55,3,17,NULL,1),(56,4,17,NULL,1),(57,5,17,NULL,1),(58,6,17,'We will use all methods of Covid 19 prevention methods like wearing mask, distancing,   sanitizers ...',1),(63,2,20,'Participants may not trust and fully share his live experience, which will affect the quality of our data.',1),(64,5,20,NULL,1),(65,6,20,'Both data collectors and study participants should wear mask in addition to maintain 4m distance between study participants and data collector in addition of wearing face mask to reduce the risk of Covid-19 transmission',1),(66,2,21,NULL,1),(67,5,21,NULL,1),(68,6,21,'All COVID-19 PREVENETION and control method will be applied during data collection',1),(73,2,24,'Since the study participants are students of high school, it is impossible to use virtual data collection approach. However, we try to use all covid prevention mechanisms.',1),(74,5,24,NULL,1),(75,6,24,'All investigators will be following the COVID guidelines while we are participating in this research.',1),(76,2,25,'reviewing patient medical records from COVID-19 treatment centers. the reason we have chosen this method is because most of the medical record data in our treatment centers is not digitalized.',1),(77,5,25,NULL,1),(78,6,25,'social distancing\r\napplying sanitizers\r\nwearing mask while collecting data',1),(101,2,37,'our study requires sample collection and indirectly involved in diagnosing patients.',1),(102,4,37,NULL,1),(103,6,37,'data collection and sample withdrawal will be handled mainly by the medical team which is already in place. data collection will be conducted in  the patients room assigned by the hospital. All research person will follow infection prevention protocols',1),(124,2,48,NULL,1),(125,4,48,NULL,1),(126,6,48,'Quantitative Data collection and measurement\r\nEight nurses will collect data using structured questionnaires through one-to-one interview of the participants at their homes. The questionnaire will include socio-demographic variables, obstetric history, HBM constructs. Data on socio-demographic and obstetric characteristics will be collected at the baseline, whereas, data on MUAC, HBM constructs will be taken before and after implementation of the interventions. Four supervisors who have MPH will supervise the research project.  Data collectors and supervisors will be trained for three days using a training manual focused on the data collection tools, procedures, and ethical issues. To prevent the breaching of privacy of the women, no one will be allowed to have access to the place where the interview is conducted. The supervisors and the principal investigator will closely follow the data collection procedure. The data collection team will hold a daily meeting to discuss challenges encountered during the day. Besides, nutrition counselors and their supervisors will hold a monthly meeting to discuss difficulties during nutrition counseling and feedback will be given to the counselors. The outcome of this trial will be the nutritional status of the pregnant Adolescents that will be assessed by measuring MUAC. Adolescents who will not attend all counseling sessions will be considered as ‘did not adhere- to the guideline’ and those who will withdraw from participating in the study will be taken as ‘lost to follow up’. Mid upper arm circumference measurements/ MUAC is a better indicator of pre-pregnancy body fat and the nutritional status of pregnant than body mass index and there is minimal change in MUAC during pregnanc. Therefore, in this study, MUAC will be used to assess the nutritional status of pregnant Adolescents. MUAC will be measured on the upper left arm. Then the distance from the acromion to olecranon processes will be measured and the midpoint will be marked. Finally, measuring tape will be placed snugly around the arm at the midpoint mark while hanging arm freely, palm facing towards the thigh. The wealth index of the household will be determined using principal component analysis (PCA) by considering latrine, water source, household assets, livestock, and agricultural land ownership. Quintiles of the wealth score will be created using the first principal component. \r\nWeight and Height Measurement\r\nThe weight will be measured using digital bath balance, Seca, which is German model for weight measurement will be used.  portable standing scale which will be calibrated on regular basis against known weight On height measuring board, Height in cm will be marked on a wall with a help of a measuring tape. All study subjects will be measured against the wall without foot wear and with heels together and their heads positioned and eyes looking straight ahead (Frankfurt plane) so that the line of vision will be perpendicular to the body and wood scale will be brought down to the top most point on the head. The adolescent should stand up straight, with buttocks, shoulder blades, and heels together touching the back of the stadiometer.\r\nQualitative Data collection\r\nKey Informant in-depth interview to managers and front-line health care providers will be used for this qualitative study. A trained graduate research assistant will conduct in-person baseline interview. Data will be collected by recording interviews by audiotape. Brief field notes will be taken during interviews. Field notes will be carefully taken during data collection and analysis. These notes will collect observations and assumptions about what will be heard or observed and personal narratives about what will be felt by the researcher during an interview.\r\nParticipants will be selected purposefully with maximum variation in age, position, type of profession place of residence (urban or rural), and educational level. Data will be collected through face-to-face in-depth interviews conducted by first author who is a PhD fellow.\r\nConsideration of covid  in the data collection process\r\nThe study will be conducted with  face-to-face interviews with adequate physical distancing and face masking and using sanitizers will allow the conduct the study. Given the situation, necessary precautions will be taken based on the recommendation of the Ethiopian FMoH and WHO to meet the timeframe and complete the study without affecting the quality of the data.',1),(127,2,49,'Most participants has no internet access ,and there is anthropometric measurement.',1),(128,4,49,NULL,1),(129,6,49,'The study will be conducted with  face-to-face interviews with adequate physical distancing and face masking and using sanitizers will allow the conduct the study. Given the situation, necessary precautions will be taken based on the recommendation of the Ethiopian FMoH and WHO to meet the timeframe and complete the study without affecting the quality of the data\r\nThe study has anthropometric measurement',1),(130,2,50,'Laboratory samples are needed',1),(131,3,50,NULL,1),(132,6,50,'Individuals suspected of COVID-19 may be included in the study. Nasal swabs to diagnose SARS-CoV-2 infection may also be collected from participants. However, all the specimen and data collection procedures will follow all standard precautions recommended by Ministry of Health of Ethiopia',1),(133,2,51,NULL,1),(134,5,51,NULL,1),(135,6,51,'No mass collection of people during data collection, distance will be kept to optimum at most convenient place between the interviewee and the interviewer, COVID-19 protection equipment such as mask and sanitizer will be used. Women having symptoms of COVID-19 will be approached with higher protection and they will be linked to health facility for screening for COVID-19',1),(136,2,52,'Since our study is a prospective cohort study on cholera exposed under fifteen years of age children with their control group in the community and some of the variables need physical contact to measure. Most of the cholera hotspot areas in which, the data will be collected are located in the periphery part of the country that has network accesses problem. So, it is not possible to collect data other than face-to-face methods.',1),(137,5,52,NULL,1),(138,6,52,'The investigators and data collectors will be following the COVID-19 guidelines while you are participating. You will be expected to wear a mask during participation and we will ask that you wash your hands (sanitize your hands, use the hand gel provided, etc.) before and after participation. Both masks and sanitizer materials well are availed by the researcher\'s expenses and we will follow the guidelines for shared items, which in this case include this consent form, the paper survey, and pen/pencil as well. This COVID-19 protocol may change at any time, based on the current recommendations from local and state departments of public health. Please feel free to ask the researchers about the COVID prevention guidelines before or during your participation, and know that you are free to withdraw or stop your participation at any time.',1),(139,2,53,'Since our study is a prospective cohort study on cholera exposed under fifteen years of age children with their control group in the community and some of the variables need physical contact to measure. Most of the cholera hotspot areas in which, the data will be collected are located in the periphery part of the country that has network accesses problem. So, it is not possible to collect data other than face-to-face methods.',1),(140,5,53,NULL,1),(141,6,53,'The investigators and data collectors will be following the COVID-19 guidelines while you are participating. You will be expected to wear a mask during participation and we will ask that you wash your hands (sanitize your hands, use the hand gel provided) before and after participation. Both masks and sanitizer materials will be availed by the researcher expenses and we will follow the guidelines for shared items, which in this case include this consent form, the paper survey, and pen/pencil as well. This COVID-19 protocol may change at any time, based on the current recommendations from local and state departments of public health. Please feel free to ask the researchers about the COVID prevention guidelines before or during your participation, and know that you are free to withdraw or stop your participation at any time.',1),(142,2,54,'Low risk of COVID-19',1),(143,5,54,NULL,1),(144,6,54,'Face masks and hand hygiene protocols will be maintained',1),(145,2,55,'the study participants are unable to use internet and have no access to internet',1),(146,5,55,NULL,1),(147,6,55,'in order to reduce the transmission of CoVID-19, the PI will provide face mask and alcohol based hand rub sanitizers to the data collectors',1),(148,2,56,'Because it is more convenient',1),(149,5,56,NULL,1),(150,6,56,'Face masks and hand sanitizers will be used consistently!',1),(151,2,57,NULL,1),(152,3,57,NULL,1),(153,6,57,'no',1),(154,2,58,'The study participants  will be selected after they come for Maternal and child health services in health facilities.',1),(155,4,58,NULL,1),(156,6,58,'The data collection process will follow the National COVID-19 guidelines and hospital protocols like using face-masking, distance,  using of sanitizers, and hand washings  etc..',1),(157,2,59,NULL,1),(158,4,59,NULL,1),(159,6,59,'All data collectors will be following the UD COVID guidelines. They will be wear a mask during data collection and sanitize their hands, use hand glove before and after practice.  They will follow the guidelines for shared items, which in this case include this consent form, the paper survey, and pen/pencil as well.  This COVID-19 protocol may change at any time, based on the current recommendations from local and state departments of public health.',1),(160,2,60,NULL,1),(161,3,60,NULL,1),(162,6,60,'All data collectors will be following the UD COVID guidelines. They will be wear a mask during data collection and sanitize their hands, use hand glove before and after practice.  They will follow the guidelines for shared items, which in this case include this consent form, the paper survey, and pen/pencil as well.  This COVID-19 protocol may change at any time, based on the current recommendations from local and state departments of public health.',1);
