ange during COVID-19 pandemic among the Adult Population in Jimma town?'),(52,15,'To determine a change in physical activity during COVID-19 pandemic among the Adult Population in Jimma town?'),(53,15,'To identify the determinants of sleep quality change during COVID-19 pandemic among the Adult Population in Jimma town?'),(54,15,'To identify determinants of change in Depression, anxiety and  stress among community in Jimma town'),(55,16,'1.	To determine of knowledge and perceptions about congenital anomalies and associated factors among married women in Jimma Zone, Ethiopia: Exploratory mixed method study'),(56,16,'2.	To explore the lived experiences of mothers or caregivers of children with congenital anomalies in Jimma context, Ethiopia: Phenomenological study'),(57,16,'3.	To explore stigma, discrimination, and social inequalities associated with congenital anomalies in Jimma context, Ethiopia: A descriptive qualitative study'),(58,17,'1.	To assess social support and associated risk factors among pregnant women in primary health care facilities, in Jimma'),(59,18,'1.	To explore patient health-literacy system, dimensions, platform, opportunities, and challenges in public-private hospital and health center contexts'),(60,18,'2.	To assess patients’ health literacy status and its cognitive, behavioral and emotional and emerging attributes'),(61,18,'3.	To describe provider and patient-related health care errors in public-private hospital/PHC settings'),(62,18,'4.	To develop and validate comprehensive patient health-literacy framework in public and private hospital settings and health centers'),(63,19,'1.	To improve compliance to evidence-based criteria in the context of PFMT during pregnancy and postpartum in Jimma Zone Hospitals.'),(64,19,'2.	To explore barriers and facilitators for engaging health professionals in PFMT as part of pre- and postnatal care program activities and to develop strategies to address areas of non-compliance.'),(65,19,'3.	To improve health pro