%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">500</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:14%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">9*500</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:11%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">4, 500</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:2px solid black; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:7%\">\r\n			<ol start=\"5\">\r\n				<li style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</li>\r\n			</ol>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; vertical-align:top; width:13%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Professional fee </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:21%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">-data analysis and report writing </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:11%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Number </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:6%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">4</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:13%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">20,000</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:14%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">4*20,000</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:11%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">80, 000</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:2px solid black; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:7%\">\r\n			<p style=\"margin-left:30px; text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; vertical-align:top; width:13%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:21%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Subtotal <sub>3</sub></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:57%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">84, 530</span></span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td rowspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:2px solid black; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:22px; width:7%\">\r\n			<ol start=\"6\">\r\n				<li style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</li>\r\n			</ol>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td rowspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:22px; vertical-align:top; width:13%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Total</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:22px; width:67%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Total</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:22px; width:11%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">162,680</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:67%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Contingency (10%)</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:25px; width:11%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">16,268</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:23px; width:67%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Grand total</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:2px solid black; border-top:none; height:23px; width:11%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><u><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">177, 948</span></span></u></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15,15,9,26,'Abstract / Executive summary\r\nThe coronavirus disease (COVID-19) pandemic has led to life-changing challenges among people across the globe. Unhealthy lifestyle habits such as poor diet, lack of physical activity, smoking, and alcohol use are the major contributors to the global burden of disease. Appropriate lifestyle changes in regard to nutrition, exercise, and sleep may help to shift the population distribution of infection risk and aid in preventing severe COVID-19 disease. While acting to control the COVID-19 pandemic, there was negligence in mitigating the risk of future chronic disease. The early identification of chronic disease at the community level is crucial in preventing the future public health problem. This study will assess the level of change in lifestyle during the COVID-19 pandemic among the Jimma town adult community and it will identify determinants of its change. A community-based cross-sectional study will be conducted from January to May 2022 in adults of Jimma town. A total of 605 samples will be selected and after proportional allocation for the selected Kebeles, individuals will be enrolled in the study by systematic sampling techniques. The data will be collected by structured and interviewer-administered questionnaires. Data will be entered into Epidata Manager 4.0.2 and exported to SPSS Version 24 analyses. A paired t-test will be used for our analysis of healthy lifestyle change before and during the COVID-19 period, and the confidence interval was set at 95%. The p-value will be two-sided, and statistical significance was set at p<0.05. Determinants of lifestyle change will be identified by using binary and multivariate logistic regression. Variables less than 0.25 on a binary will be a candidate for multivariate logistic regression. A cutoff point of p-value less than 0.05 will declare a statistically significant association on multivariate logistic regression.  The result will be reported in the form of tables and graphs. The total required budget will be 269,500.00ETB.','Determinants of healthy lifestyle changes','Determinants of healthy lifestyle changes during COVID-19 pandemic among the Adult Population in Jimma town: A community based cross-sectional study','2021-11-19 10:38:44','4.13 Research outcome and output\r\nThis project will come up with any detected changes in healthy lifestyle among the community in Jimma town. In early action to these changes is by identification of determinants of those changes which will be identified by this project. Individual-based healthy lifestyle recommendations will be delivered to the participants and this will be the immediate outcome of this project. This research will have a variety of outcomes in many phases. It has an immediate outcome in revealing the burden to those in need of action. It will give a focus on health policy planning. Over the long run, an unhealthy lifestyle will result in a future chronic disease burden. Therefore, the output of this study will help in preventing this expected outcome in many ways.','3bc87e58d1233482b2648a0934b33c5d','completed','1 . Background and Rationale of the study\r\nThe Coronavirus disease (COVID-19) pandemic has brought demanding situations and adjustments to human existence worldwide, inflicting an unrivaled effect on human health, lifestyle, and social existence, and has affected the neighborhood and worldwide economy. It has caused challenges especially on lifestyle change amongst humans throughout the globe. Social distancing and self-isolation have become a reality. As humans have been looking to adapt to this new challenge, the confinement has notably impacted citizens’ lives bringing approximately a surprising and radical extrude of their routine activities and lifestyle(1, 2). The lockdown time has led to disrupted food intake patterns, low stages of physical activity, perceived weight all of which boom the hazard of obese and obesity(3). Appropriate lifestyle adjustments in regard to nutrition, exercise, and sleep can shift the population distribution of infection and useful resources in stopping severe COVID-19 disease(4).\r\nCOVID-19 is an international burden that maintains to redefines everyday lifestyle-associated conduct in a great way because the pandemic progresses via its different phases.  Public health and government measures are taken to prevent infection have indirectly impacted dietary quality, daily activities, and access to recreational settings. These changes if extended over a long run, to appreciably extrude lifestyle-associated behaviors, in particular everyday eating, bodily activities, and sleep behaviors which might be recognized to be independent risk factors for metabolic complications such as obesity, diabetes, and cardiovascular disorders(5–7). According to CDC, food plans, weight management, bodily activity, stress, and sleep habit are the foremost components of a healthy lifestyle (8–10).\r\nMaintaining ordinary PA in the self-isolation period has a double significance in the prevention of future chronic health conditions due to a sedentary lifestyle. (11). Regular physical activity (PA) is an important protection for the prevention and treatment of major chronic non-communicable diseases (NCDs). Especially heart disease, diabetes, stroke, and breast and colon cancer. Moreover, It also prevents other important NCD risk factors such as hypertension, overweight, and obesity, and is associated with improved mental health and improved quality of life. Beyond health, increasing participation in physical activity has a significant contribution in achieving the 2030 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)(12).\r\nGlobally, 23% of adults and 81% of adolescents do not meet the WHO global recommendations on physical activity for health. Notably, the prevalence of inactivity varies extensively inside and among countries, and maybe as excessive as 80% in some adult populations(12). Scaling up levels of PA may partly decrease the severity of COVID-19 disease. Some dietary patterns consumption as well as drinking less tea were correlated reduced severity of disease(13). COVID-19 confinement had a negative impact on PA levels and exacerbated sedentary behaviors(14). \r\n\r\nUnhealthy lifestyle habits include a poor diet, physical inactivity, and some behavioral factors are major and important contributors to the global burden of disease but are also positively associated with worse mental health outcomes. Recently, lifestyle such as healthy nutritional status and involvement in physical exercise at home during the COVID-19 outbreak was recommended (15–17). Adult people are suffering tremendously with their sleep quality during the pandemic(18). Sleep disturbances were prevalent among 60.8% of the participants during the pandemic(19). The burden of sleep disorders during the COVID-19 pandemic affects approximately 40% of adults from general populations. In patients with active COVID-19, the prevalence rates of sleep problems were higher(20). Lockdown measures increased sleep complaints and resulted in sleep abnormality among pre-pandemic good sleepers(21). \r\n\r\nSo far, many negative lifestyle behaviors have been manifested during COVID-19(22). Drinking, smoking, exercise, nutrition, and stress are also elements of lifestyle according to the WHO’s definition of the term. Previous studies have highlighted the importance of healthy lifestyles as they are crucial in maintaining and improving physical and mental health and improving the quality of life(23,24). According to the research evidence, several lifestyle factors become frequent adults during the COVID-19 pandemic period(25).\r\nSmoking cessation awareness is strongly encouraged as a public health measure to limit the global impact of COVID-19, which was found to increase up to 31.1% during the pandemic (26,27).  It will increase the transmission of the COVID-19 virus and it was considered as a risk factor for the disease transmission. A Negative change was reported for physical activity, sleep, alcohol, and smoking in 48.9%, 40.7%, 26.6%,  and 6.9% respectively in the adult population of Australia during the pandemic(27). The general population is utilizing alcohol and substances, potentially as a means of coping with the pandemic (28). This will in turn associated with higher depression, anxiety, and stress among future populations(29).\r\nLifestyle chance has a double impact on the health of the population. Its immediate effect may range from individual discomfort, decrease in productivity, sleep disturbance, and increase in the risk of acute and chronic disease. In long run, it will lead to the development of an unhealthy lifestyle which will affect the diverse and multidimensional life of the community, including the emerging of chronic non-communicable disease as a major public health problem upon the existing burden. While acting to control the COVID-19 pandemic, there was negligence in mitigating the risk of future increment in chronic disease. The early identification of those factors that may lead the community to this risk is crucial in controlling the future public health problem. This study will assess the level of change in healthy lifestyle among Jimma town adult community and will identify determinants of its change.','4 . Design and methods\r\n4. 1 Study Area and Period\r\nThe study will be conducted in adults≥ 18 years living in Jimma Town, which is located 352km away from Addis Ababa, to the southwest of Ethiopia. The town currently consists of seventeen Kebeles (The lowest administrative unit). According to population projection of 2017 at zonal and Woreda levels, a total population was 195,228; among these 97,259 are male and 97,969 are women. The study will be commenced from 15th March 2021 to 15th May 2021. \r\n4.2 Study Design\r\nA community-based cross-sectional study design will be employed.\r\n4.3 Population\r\nSource population: All adults ≥ 18 years living in Jimma town during the study period.\r\nStudy population: Adults ≥ 18 years in Jimma Town selected into the study.\r\nInclusion and exclusion criteria: All adults in Jimma Town ≥ 18 will be included. Those with a diagnosis of a severe coexisting medical problem that would prevent participation would be excluded. Pregnant women will be excluded from the study. \r\n\r\n\r\n4.4 Sampling procedure and Sample size estimation\r\nA systematic sampling technique will be used to identify study participants and a single proportion of population formulas will be used to calculate the sample size. Accordingly, \r\nn=[(Zα/2)2*p(1-p) ]/d2	Where, \r\np= Expected population proportion of the vaccine acceptance \r\nd= degree of absolute precision/ error tolerated (0.05) \r\nZ α/2= Standard normal variable at 95% Confidence level (1.96).\r\nBy taking the anticipated prevalence of the vaccine acceptance 50%, a total of 384 samples will be enrolled. 5 % non response rate considered and design effect (1.5) will be employed result in final sample size of (384+39=422) *1.5 = 634.\r\nThe selection of these Kebeles will be done according to World Health Organization criteria of at least 30% of the cluster in conducting survey study. Therefore, thirty percent of seventeen Kebeles become approximately six Kebeles and systematic sampling will be applied to select households.  A multi-stage (combination of SRS and systematic) sampling technique will be utilized. Initially, 6 Kebeles were selected from the 17 Kebeles of the town by simple random sampling, and then the total sample size of 605 will be distributed to the six Kebeles employing proportional to size allocation to the Kebeles. An individual from the household will be then chosen with a lottery method. \r\n4.5 Data collection tools\r\nData collection tool will be developed by different literature search including(1), and it includes the following components socio-demographic characteristics, behavioral factors, medical conditions, and different factors which will help us to assess basic healthy lifestyle (feeding habit, physical activity, and sleep habit of an individual)components of an individual. Lifestyle will be assessed by the standard tool of Yonsei Lifestyle Questionnaire English version. Physical activity participation per week beforehand after the onset of COVID-19. The six physical activities include aerobic physical activity; anaerobic physical activity; low-intensity physical activity equivalent to 2–2.9 metabolic equivalent of task (MET), including gardening, house cleaning, etc.; moderate-intensity physical activity equivalent to 3–5.9 MET, including swimming, doubles tennis, etc.; high-intensity physical activity equivalent to 6–9.9MET, such as running, climbing, etc.; and walking exercises. Depression Anxiety Stress Scale 21 (DASS-21) questionnaires will be used for the assessment of DAS.\r\n4.6 Study variables\r\nDependent Variable: Lifestyle change (physical activity, eating habit, depression, anxiety, stress, and sleep condition)\r\nIndependent Variable\r\n	Sociodemographic factors: age, sex, religion, education status, marital status, occupation, income, and family size \r\n	Physical measurements: weight, height, BMI, Hip circumference, Waist circumference, and blood pressure \r\n	Behavioral  Characteristics: smoking status/ tobacco use, alcohol consumption, chat chewing, physical activity, and level of stress\r\n	Medical conditions: Hypertension, Diabetes Mellitus, and Cardiovascular disease\r\n	Social factors \r\n	Pandemic related factors\r\n4.7 Operational definition\r\n	Lifestyle change: a significant change in one of feeding habit, physical activity, depression, anxiety, stress, and sleep quality, and substance use. \r\n4.8 Data management and statistical analysis\r\nData will be entered into Epi Data Manager 4.0.2(Odense, Denmark) and exported to SPSS Version 24 (SPSS, Chicago, IL, USA) for statistical analysis. The results of the questionnaire surveys will be summarized and reported using frequency and percentage. To determine changes in lifestyle due to COVID-19, this study will calculate the descriptive statistics of indicators that will be measured before and after the pandemic. A paired t-test will be used for our analysis of healthy lifestyle change before and during the COVID-19 period, and the confidence interval was set at 95%. The p-value will be two-sided, and statistical significance was set at p<0.05. All statistical analyses were performed using SPSS software version 24. Determinants of lifestyle change will be identified by using binary and multivariate logistic regression. Variables less than 0.25 on a binary will be a candidate for multivariate logistic regression. A cutoff point of p-value less than 0.05 will declare a statistically significant association on multivariate logistic regression.  The result will be reported in the form of tables and graphs.\r\n4.9 Quality assurance\r\nThe pre-test will be conducted on 5% of the study population (in adults living in Agaro town) before the actual date of data collection and modification of the data collection tool will be conducted based on the result of the pre-test. Data will be collected by trained data collectors and it will be supervised by experienced supervisors. Before the data analysis, the raw data will be checked for missing, completeness and also double entry will be performed to minimize error.\r\n\r\n4.10Plan for dissemination and ensuring utilization of findings\r\n\r\nThe result of this study will be presented to the Jimma University Emergency Operation Centre and Institute of Health Research Directorate. An effort will be made to publish the result in peer-reviewed reputable journals. The result of the study will also be distributed to the community and the town health office and health professionals through newspapers, bulletins, and pamphlets in major languages spoken in the town.\r\n4.11 Ethical and environmental considerations\r\nEthical clearance for the study will be obtained from the Jimma University Institute of Health, Institutional Review Board (IRB). Written permission will be obtained from the Jima town administration to undertake the study in the town. The study will be performed after informed written consent is obtained from the study participant and data collection will be conducted confidentially. The different steps in the data collection process will be carefully explained to the participants and also assured that they could withdraw from the study at any time if they so desired. All the necessary preparation will be arranged to prevent COVID-19 transmission during the time of data collection.\r\n4.12 Capacity building\r\n	Two masters students will be involved in the project','<h1><span style=\"font-size:16pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">References&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></h1>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot