tom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid #4f81bd; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:208px; vertical-align:top; width:150px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Build &ldquo;Begena&rdquo; sounds database</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:208px; vertical-align:top; width:138px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">January 21 ,2022-Feburary 21, 2022</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:208px; vertical-align:top; width:162px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Investigate different &ldquo;Begena&rdquo; melodies and create a database. </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:208px; vertical-align:top; width:240px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*Team up skilled professional</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*Prepare Begena instrument and other recording material for study </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*Record Begena instrumental sound at a study frequency range at Jimma university music school studio </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid #4f81bd; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:150px; vertical-align:top; width:150px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Administration of Begena Sound to subject and EEG signal recording </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:150px; vertical-align:top; width:138px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">February 22, 2022 -June15, 2022 </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:150px; vertical-align:top; width:162px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Testing to see to see its treatment effectiveness, reliability, and practically feasible</span></span> </span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:150px; vertical-align:top; width:240px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*Team up skilled professional</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> Administer &ldquo;Begena&rdquo; to subjects</span></span> </span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">* EEG signal recording of both control and case group </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:1px solid #4f81bd; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:83px; vertical-align:top; width:150px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">EEG-based Neural Signal Analysis</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">and Interpretation </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:83px; vertical-align:top; width:138px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">June 16,2022- July 15, 2022 </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:83px; vertical-align:top; width:162px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Frequency-Domain EEG Signal Analysis&nbsp; </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:83px; vertical-align:top; width:240px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*Selection of proper software </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*Follow-up proposed methodology and analyze EEG-Signal </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:1px solid #4f81bd; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:68px; vertical-align:top; width:150px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Publication and reporting of new finding and result</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:68px; vertical-align:top; width:138px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">July 16 ,2022 &ndash; September&nbsp; 20 , 2022</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:68px; vertical-align:top; width:162px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Documentation&nbsp; and publication of final progress </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"background-color:#fde9d9; border-bottom:1px solid #4f81bd; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid #4f81bd; border-top:none; height:68px; vertical-align:top; width:240px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Cambria&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Reporting final progress to JU-innovation and research director office and publication of new finding on international journal</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><strong>Total Requested Budget: 240,000ETB</strong></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><strong>Project duration : about 10 month Des 20,2021 to Sep 20, 2022 GC</strong></span></li>\r\n</ul>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(22,116,9,19,'Background: Antimicrobial resistance (AMR) remains a main problem in the 21st century. It is one of the most serious disasters that jeopardize the global public health. Recent studies suggest that antibiotic resistance rate especially cephalosporins drugs increased dramatically. But, there is no data on antimicrobial resistance profile of cephalosporin drugs and the contributing factors in Jimma private Hospitals. Hence, the objective of this study is to determine the susceptibility pattern of the common clinical isolates against cephalosporin drugs and the main contributing factors for drug resistance in various health institutions located in Jimma town.\r\nMethods: A health facility based cross sectional study will be conducted from February to December, 2022 in various Hospitals located in Jimma town. Prospective study will be carried out to assess the knowledge and practice of cephalosporin drugs prescription and resistance. In addition, retrospective study will be conducted to evaluate the utilization pattern of the same drugs.  Moreover, the quality of these drugs will be evaluated based on different parameters such as assay, dissolution, friability etc. using HPLC, Dissolution apparatus, fraibrator, etc.   Finally, susceptibly test will be carried out to determine the current resistance pattern of cephalosporins.  Accordingly, the clinical isolates will be collected by professional nurses from hospitalized patients in different wards of the hospital. After the inoculums were standardized and inoculated on gar plate, sterile antibiotic discs will be equidistantly placed and incubated at appropriate condition and time. Finally, zone of inhibition will be measured and interpreted.\r\nResults: the finding of the study will be presented using texts, graphs and tables.\r\nConclusion and recommendations: An appropriate conclusion will be drown based on the finding of the study and the recommendations will be forwarded. \r\nTimeline: The study will be conducted in 12 months (February to December, 2022).\r\nBudget summary. This research proposal is divided into two phases (Phase 1 = 226875 birr and Phase two= 405207 birr). Thus a total of 632,082 Ethiopian birr will be spent',NULL,'Evaluation of Antimicrobial resistance of clinical isolates against cephalosporin drugs and the contributing factors in various health institution of Jimma town','2021-11-19 13:15:09','6.	Research output/ Outcome \r\nThis study will reveal the prevalence of the resistance pattern of the cephalosporin drugs in Jimma health institution. Moreover it tells us the quality level of the cephalosporin drugs marketed in Ethiopia and the utilization pattern of these drugs. Subsequently, this comprehensive finding will help the regulatory body to initiate rule and regulation to tackle the observed problems. It also used as an input for the prescribers to follow appropriate treatment modality selection, initiate other researchers to conduct drug quality test of this group. Further, this study is essential for any responsible body to see the gaps and works on rational use of antibiotics to decrease emergency of resistant bacteria strain, by improving proper use, proper indication, proper dose, proper duration and frequency.','5a743c847b5410f4ff5a1758ca895723','completed','Background  \r\nFollowing modern medicines, Antibiotics have always been considered as one of the wonder discoveries of the 20th century. Among them, cephalosporin is the largest and most diverse family of beta-lactam antibiotics. They are structurally and pharmacologically related to the penicillin’s [1]. Among the various generations of cephalosporin   drugs ceftriaxone, which is the member of the “third generation”, characterized by a relatively broad antibacterial spectrum, including moderate activity against many strains of Pseudomonas aeruginosa. In addition to its broad antibacterial spectrum, ceftriaxone exhibits a uniquely long elimination half-life, resistant to β-lactamase producing organisms among third generations, and diffuses well into extravascular spaces, including the cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) [1-2]. Otherwise all cephalosporin drugs exhibit the same characteristics.  \r\nEven though the use of ceftriaxone is more predominant other groups of cephalosporin are still in use due to their nature of broad spectrum against multiple bacteria. These characteristics offer potential clinical advantages which may lead to increasing use of this drug to treat bacterial meningitis and a variety of other serious infections [2-3].\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFigure 1: Chemical structure of Cephalosporin \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFollowing patient diagnosis choosing of drugs in the management of any disease is an important point of consideration to the healthcare practitioners and the probability of looking for antimicrobials is paramount, especially in developing countries like Ethiopia [4, 5]. \r\n\r\nAnti-microbial resistance (AMR) due to the over and incorrect use of antimicrobials is one of the threatening issues of public health [6]. The contributing factors for antibiotics resistance includes incorrect medicine choices, incorrect dose, prescribing drugs that cause ADRs or drug interactions, use of poor quality drugs, and the use of expensive drugs when cheaper ones would be possible [7].As a result, several stakeholders at every corner of the globe are striving to conduct research to assess, predictors of drug resistance, resistance level, stimulate policies and actions in the healthcare system [8].\r\n Recent studies suggest that antibiotic resistance rate especially for cephalosporins drugs including cefotaxime and ceftazidime increased dramatically [9]. In Ethiopia, there is an increased and multiple drug resistance to the currently available antimicrobial drugs [10] A high prevalence of antibiotic resistant staphylococcus aureus and Escherichia coli strains was observed in the country ([11 \r\n\r\nA verbally claimed from many other health professions is there on the misuse of cephalosporin at private clinic and hospitals. Especially third generation cephalosporin is more common types of this group to abuse with particularity on ceftriaxone. Therefor assessing practice and attitude of prescriber towards cephalosporin antibiotics and conducting susceptibility study with analytical quality study is mandatory. More over the retrospective cross sectional study on selected cephalosporin is found very crucial. \r\nRATIONALE OF THE STUDY \r\nData on AMR among local pathogens help define the best possible treatment for individual patients [12]. However, the proportion of resistant bacteria can vary from one area to another, and in many health facilities there are no data on resistance patterns. Experiences from surveillance networks on antimicrobial use and AMR show that, data were available, can be put to multiple uses, including orienting treatment choices, understanding AMR trends, informing public health policy, identifying priority areas for interventions, and monitoring the impact of interventions to contain resistance [11]. \r\n\r\nAt present, there is no data on antimicrobial resistance profile of cephalosporin drugs in Ethiopia.  Recently, cephalosporins are the drugs indicated for severe systemic infections caused by gram positive and gram negative bacteria [13]. So, the current antimicrobial resistance surveillance will have a great impact to improve and advance the current infection control programs in the hospital to prevent the spread of resistant microorganisms.\r\n\r\nThe main factor behind the escalating resistance at a population and individual level could be antibiotic misuse and inappropriate prescribing [14, 15].  The knowledge and practice of physicians toward the prescribing of these drugs could be a contributing factors for antimicrobial resistance [15 ].  \r\nThus, understanding the knowledge and practices of physicians towards antibiotic resistance is key for interventions to tackle antimicrobial resistance. Moreover,   Implementation of antimicrobial stewardship programs (ASP) lies at the core of optimizing appropriate use of antibiotics in healthcare facilities. There have been no studies conducted toward the knowledge and practice of prescription and drug resistance among prescribers in the current study setting.   Therefore, one of the aims of this study will be to investigate physicians’ knowledge and practice towards antibiotic prescriptions and resistance. \r\n\r\nThe inclusion of private Hospital in Jimma is make  more valuable as it has been not conducted before on private clinic across the country. Therefore, as drug using pattern in the private Hospitals is quite distinct from governmental or public health facility and oral complains is arisen from customer and from some other health professionals, this study paramount important. Thus this study will present the susceptibility level of this groups of drugs, and different brands quality study using HPLC, assess the practice and attitude of prescribers towards the selected drugs, and retrospective cross sectional study. \r\nTherefore, from this study the main predictors for antimicrobial resistance and elucidating the antimicrobial resistant profile of clinical isolates against of cephalosporin drugs which are commonly prescribed for treatment of severe infectious diseases will be present.','3.1.	Materials \r\nMaterials/ reagent / chemicals \r\nCeftriaxone reference standard, other cephalosporin reference standard,   acetonitrile soudium hydroxide, sodium hydrogen monobasic salt, different stern of standard bacteria,  sterile  distilled  or cold boiled water, sodium hydroxide solution, iodine and Agar\r\nEquipment \r\nHigh performance liquid chromatograph (HPLC), dissolution apparatus,  pH meter, analytical balance, centrifuge, refrigerator, laboratory disc,  etc. \r\n3.2.	Assessment of the knowledge and the prescribing practices of cephalosporin drugs among prescribers in all hospital in Jimma town\r\n3.2.1.	Study area\r\nThe study will be carried out in various health institutions including both the government and private hospitals located in Jimma town. Thus, Jimma medical center, Huleoda hospital, Jimma Awetu hospital, Shene gibe hospital  and Firomisis Hospital will be included in the current study March to May, 2022. \r\n3.2.2.	Study design and population\r\nA Heath facility based cross sectional study will be conducted in selected health institutions located in Jimma town. All the health professionals who are working in the selected health institutions will be used as source of population. The study population will be all the prescribers who are working at different wards of the selected health institutions.\r\n3.2.3.	Sampling technique and Sample size\r\nA convenient sampling technique will be used to enroll the prescribers available at the selected health institutions during the data collection period until the required sample size is obtained. The number of respondents will be allocated to each health institutions based on the proportions of the prescribers working at each health service center.  The sample size is calculated based on the single proportion formula in which n= sampe size, p= the estimated prevalence based on previous WHO estimation, which is 0.5, w = maximum allow able error = 0.05 and Z = value of standard normal distribution (Z-statistic) at 95% confidence level and which is 1.96. Thus, the computed sample size with 10% non-response/non-volunteers rate became: 217+ 22(10%) =239\r\n\r\n3.2.4.	 Data collection\r\nThe questioners are developed after reviewing various relevant literatures. So, structured standardized self-administered questionnaire will distributed to the study participants by trained data collectors. The questionnaire has mainly three parts: (1) Implementation of antibiotic steward-ship programs in selected hospitals and prior training on antibiotic prescribing practice and antibiotic drug resistance (2) Demographic and occupational characteristics of study participants (3) Knowledge, and practice of antibiotic prescriptions and resistance. The questionnaires will be pretested prior to its application for data collection.\r\n3.3.	A Retrospective Study Assessment of Cephalosporin Utilization in Different Wards of private Hospital in   Jimma town. \r\n3.3.1.	Study area\r\nThe study will be conducted in all private hospital wards located in Jimma town. Thus, Huleoda hospital, Jimma Awetu hospital, and Firomisis Hospital will be included in the current study March to May, 2022\r\n\r\n3.3.2.	Study design and population\r\nA Heath facility based retrospective cross sectional study will be conducted in selected health institutions located in Jimma town. All inpatient charts records who have been admitted to any of the wards in the last years will be used as source of population. The study population will be all patient charts containing cephalosporin drug prescription in selected wards in prior to one year during data collection. \r\n3.3.3.	Sampling technique and Sample size \r\nA systematic random sampling technique will be employed.  Initially all patient chart within the study period will be counted and separately put in chart with cephalosporin medication.  Then samples will be taken every X interval from cephalosporin containing charts and the first chart was picked by lottery method. The sample size is calculated based on the single proportion formula in which n= sample size, p= the estimated prevalence based on previous WHO estimation, which is 0.5, w = maximum allow able error = 0.05 and Z = value of standard normal distribution (Z-statistic) at 95% confidence level and which is 1.96. Thus, the computed sample size with 10% non-response/non-volunteers rate became: 2778+ 28(10%) =306 \r\n. \r\n3.3.4.	Data collection procedures\r\nData construct format will be developed   based on different  guideline like  Standard Treatment Guideline (STG) of Ethiopian, WHO guidelines 2015,American Society of Health-System Pharmacists (ASHP) and Infectious Diseases Society of America (IDSA).For majority of the conditions, the STG will be  used to evaluate compliance of Cephalosporin use in terms of indication, dose, frequency and duration of treatment. Data collection Check list will be developed for this study which is based on STG of Ethiopia for Hospitals. \r\n3.3.5.	Data Collectors\r\nData collector will be recruited, and training will be provided on the purpose and the use of the data abstraction format. At the same time, they will be oriented on ethical principles of confidentiality and data management prior to their involvement.\r\n3.4.	Quality assessment of cephalosporin drug brands present in Jimma town\r\n3.4.1.	Sample size and sampling method \r\nA convenience sampling technique will be used for sample collection.  Mysterious shopping style will be used for sample collection. Different brands of cephalosporins formulations will be identified and enough amounts for the required tests will be purchased in their original package as supplied by the manufacturers from different drug retail outlets located in Jimma town. The  collected  samples  will  be  taken  to  Jimma  University  drug  quality laboratory  (JUDQL). All samples will be undergone visual and physical inspection for labelling and packaging before quality testing. The products will be coded randomly for purposes of the research and the study will be performed before product expiration dates.\r\n3.4.2.	Physicochemical propreties study of cephalosporin drugs. \r\n Among the quality parameters required for pharmaceutical product, physicochemical study  are the most common and determining quality parameters, it would be two folded when it comes to liquid dosage form. All collected cephalosporin collected will be evaluated as per the WHO requirement. \r\n\r\n3.4.3.	 Identification study\r\nThe identification test for Ceftriaxone will be done by USP method. The main peak from the chromatogram of assay analysis will take as identity of ceftriaxone as indicated in USP pharmacopeia and all chemical identification test will be conducted. \r\n3.4.4.	 Assay of ceftriaxone \r\nThe amount of each cephalosporin drug brands will be determined using high performance liquid chromatography UV / DAD detector HPLC.  Quantification will be based on calibration curve obtained, after injection of samples. The calibration curve will be established by a plot of peak versus concentration % (w/w).\r\n3.4.5.	Dissolution study of cephalosporin \r\nAmong quality parameters of tablet and capsule dosage forms dissolution are the most common types of parameters. Hence dissolution profiles of cephalosporin drugs brands will be conducted as per pharmacopeia. The recommended dissolution apparatus will be used to analyze the quality of those brands. \r\n3.4.6.	Friability and hardness study of cephalosporin drugs \r\nThe friability study will be conducted using friability apparatus as recommended standard by different pharmacopeia. The hardness study will be also conducted using hardness tester. \r\n3.5.	Determination of the susceptibility pattern of clinical isolates against cephalosporin drugs in Jimma medical center. \r\n\r\n3.5.1.	Study design and population\r\nA Heath facility based cross sectional study will be conducted in the selected health institutions located in Jimma town. All patients who visit the selected study hospital will be used as source population and the study population will be all admitted patients at different wards of the health institutions.\r\n3.5.2.	Sampling technique and Sample size\r\nClinical isolates of each strain will be collected from patients of admitted to the selected health institution. A convenient sampling technique will be used to get as much as sufficient samples containing the bacterial isolates will be obtained. All the isolates will be collected from the blood, wound swab, Sputum and urine samples of patients who are admitted to different wards. Patients who give their consent will be included in the study. Patients who do not want to participate will be excluded from the study.\r\n3.5.3.	Sample collection procedure\r\nThe nurses will be trained on how to record patient’s information and how to collect the specimens from the patients.  Urine samples will be collected and inoculated on MaConckey and blood agar, and incubated aerobically at 37 °C for 24 h. The blood agar (after sub-culturing on nutrient agar) will be tested for conventional biochemical tests: oxidase test, catalase, citrate utilization, and oxidative fermentation.  A venous blood will be collected. Blood culture broths will be incubated at 370C and checked for sign of bacterial growth daily up to 7 days, and bottles which showed signs of growth will be further processed for gram stain and sub-cultured will be made onto blood agar,MacConkey agar, manitol salt agarand incubated at 37°C for 24 hours.\r\n3.5.4.	Antimicrobial susceptibility testing\r\n3.5.4.1.	   Standardization of inoculum using direct colony suspension \r\nStandardization of the inoculum will be carried out according to the procedure described by Lalitha, M.K., 2004. The top of 2-3 colonies from the slant will be touched with a sterile inoculating loop, and the growth will be transferred into a tube containing 5ml of tryptone soya broth and incubated at 370C for 24 hours and then streaked onto tryptone soya agar; incubated at 370C for 24 hours. Prior to preparing the inoculum, the agar plates containing the test organism and control strain will be visually examined. If culture appears mixed, a fresh subculture will be prepared. At least three to five well-isolated colonies of the same morphological type will be selected from an agar plate culture and transferred into Muller Hinton broth and incubated at 370C for 24 hour. The turbidity of the suspension will be adjusted with sterile saline or broth to obtain turbidity optically comparable to that of the 0.5 McFarland standard which results in a suspension containing approximately1 to 2 x 108 CFU/ml of the bacteria. To perform this step properly it will be done visually with adequate light to compare the inoculum tube and the 0.5 McFarland standards against a card with a white background and contrasting black lines (Stephen, 2005 and EUCAST Disk Diffusion Method for Antimicrobial Susceptibility Testing, 2012).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n3.5.4.2.	 Inoculation of the preparation and application of discs to inoculated agar plates \r\nWithin 15 minutes of preparing the adjusted inoculum, a sterile cotton swab will be dipped into the inoculum and rotated several times and pressed firmly on the inside wall of the tube above the fluid level to remove excess inoculum from the swab. Then the swab will be streaked over the entire surface of the freshly prepared Mueller Hinton agar plate. Inoculation will be completed by running the swab around the rim of the agar plate. The antimicrobial disks will be applied to the plates within 15 minutes after inoculation. Sterile antibiotic discs will be equidistantly placed on these plates and gently pressed onto the medium with the help of sterile forceps to ensure complete contact with the agar surface. The plates will then be incubated at 37°C for 24hrs. A zone of inhibition will be measured in millimeters using a ruler around each antimicrobial discs and will be recorded and results will be interpreted as sensitive, resistant, or intermediate based on resistance data interpreted according to Clinical and Laboratory Standards Institute[16]. Sensitivity, intermediate resistance and resistances will be determined by the zone of complete growth inhibition around each disk [16, 17].\r\n\r\n                      Procedural algorism\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n.\r\n3.5.5.	Quality control \r\nThe reliability of the study findings will be guaranteed by implementing quality control measures throughout the whole process of the laboratory work. Reagents, drugs, culture medias and antibiotic discs will be checked for their normal shelf life before use. Proper sample and data collection and handling will be done by trained experts who are working at each stage. Results will be interpreted in accordance to the recommended Standards.\r\n3.5.6.	  Data Analysis and Interpretation\r\nData will be edited, cleaned, entered and analyzed using statistical package for social science (SPSS) version 20. The data will be interpreted based on the standard interpretive results of inhibition zone diameter nearest whole (mm) of each cephalosporin drugs for each bacterial isolates. Descriptive analysis such as frequencies and mean will be used. P-value of < 0.05 will be considered to indicate statistically significant differences and the result will be presented using tables.','<ol>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Bush K., Macielag M. J. (2010).&nbsp;New &beta;-lactam antibiotics and &beta;-lactamase inhibitors.&nbsp;Expert Opin. Ther. Pat.&nbsp;20, 1277&ndash;129310.&nbsp; </span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"background-color:white\"><span style=\"color:black\">Aminov R. I. (2009).&nbsp;The role of antibiotics and antibiotic resistance in nature.&nbsp;Environ. Microbiol.&nbsp;11, 2970&ndash;298810.&nbsp; ( for anbitbiotics discover and role)</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">Abdulghani T (2012). The Outcome of the Misuse of 3rdGeneration Cephalosporins in Fallujah City, West of Iraq. Anb Med J; Vol.10 No.2;&nbsp; pages; 46-50.</span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">National Committee for Clinical Laboratory Standards, Methods for Dilution Antimicrobial Susceptibility Tests for Bacteria that Grow Aerobically; Approved Standard-Fifth Edition. NCCLS document M7-A5 (ISBN 1-56238&shy; 309-9). NCCLS, Wayne, PA 19087-1898, 2000. ( structure of&nbsp; Ceftriaxone) </span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">Abebe&nbsp; F,&nbsp; Berhe&nbsp; D,&nbsp;&nbsp; Berhe&nbsp; A,&nbsp; Hishe&nbsp; H,&nbsp; Akaleweld&nbsp; M&nbsp; (2012).&nbsp; Drug&nbsp; Use Evaluation&nbsp; of Ceftriaxone: The Case of Ayder Referral Hospital, Mekelle, Ethiopia.&nbsp; IJPSR; Vol. 3(7): 2191-2195.</span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">&nbsp;Weinberg J. (1999) how do you choose antibiotics treatment British Medical&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Jouranl: 318 (1) 1614-1618).</span></span></span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:48px; text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ol start=\"7\">\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">Adrian B, Johan M, Mark S, Maria B (2007). Antimicrobial susceptibility profile of selected bacteraemic pathogens from private institutions in South Africa. S Afr Med J; 97:273-279. </span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">Aggarwal A, Singh A, OberoiA&nbsp; (2007). A Three-year Retrospective 