"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">25</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">,550</span></span></span> </span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:55px; vertical-align:top; width:55px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">3</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:55px; width:570px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">conduct pre-test of the application software </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:55px; vertical-align:top; width:90px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">50,000</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; width:570px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">Project related Equipment, software, materials and other supplies </span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">Phone/tablets, flash etc.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:90px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:black\">80,300</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:21px; vertical-align:top; width:55px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">4</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:21px; vertical-align:top; width:570px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Per-diem for&nbsp;&nbsp; trainees (software&nbsp; managers, hospital &nbsp;administrators&nbsp; and supervisors),</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; height:21px; vertical-align:top; width:90px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">188,000</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td rowspan=\"3\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:55px\">\r\n			<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:570px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Total </span></span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:90px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">519,850</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:570px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Contingency (10%)</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:90px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">51,985</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:570px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Grand Total </span></span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:90px\">\r\n			<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><strong><u><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">561,835.00</span></span></u></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(32,26,9,24,'Proposal summary\r\nAutism is a neurodevelopmental disorder characterized by impaired social interaction, restricted interests, compromised communication skills, repetitive patterns of behavior and unusual stereotyped interests. It is a complex, serious, biological based disorder with variety of characteristic features like hyperactivity and quick frustration to any situations, social deficits, abnormalities in communication, cognitive inflexibility, irritability, aggression, self-injury, lack of attention, and several fits of bad temper where its signs and symptoms vary from mild to profound mental retardation that coined by ‘Autism Spectrum Disorder’ (ASD) with multiple co-morbidities. The prevalence rate of ASD is steadily rising globally per year. Although there is scarcity of literatures, there is no reason to believe that rates of autism will be any less low elsewhere. In Ethiopia more than 600,000 children were estimated to live with ASD. The impact of ASD is not limited to affected children but, it also hampered quality of life of children that leads to social, psychological and spiritual impacts of families as the child with ASD is discriminated/stereotyped, hidden at home with wrong spiritual beliefs. The disease also causes significant medical expenses and majority of couples with autistic children end their marriages in divorce. The cause of ASD is multi-factorial with genetic and environmental factors. The effect of essential nutrient in the development and prognosis of ASD gets special focus area of the research. Majority of studies revealed that optimal human breast milk feeding (early initiation of breast feeding within 1 hour of delivery, exclusive breast feeding for six months and feeding for long duration) is associated with decreased risk of ASD due to the presence of adequate nutrients (essential fatty acids, insulin-like grow factor, immune factors, oxytocin, melatonin) in breast milk with numerous health benefits for physical and neurologic development, protecting from infections, better cognitive functions. It is also realized that supplementation of essential nutrients such as oral vitamin D, B2, B12, cyclo-glycylproline and essential fatty acids improve of cognitive status and communication skills of children with ASD. But, there is no study that compares the effects of multiple nutrients in improving the manifestation of the disease further. Thus, the present study aims to investigate the roles of supplementation of different essential nutrients for the prognosis of ASD. The study will be conducted at two Ethiopian autism centers (Nehemiah Autism Center and Nia foundation Joy Autism Center) both located in the capital of the country, Addis Ababa. A randomized experimental study design will be applied to assess the roles of supplementation of essential nutrients in the prognosis of ASD among children with autism at Ethiopian Autism centers. Different groups of supplementation of essential nutrients as intervention groups (G1-G6 who treated with vitamin D3, omega, docosa hexanooic acid, vitamin B12, folic acid and  vitamin A respectively with standard doses PO for 9 months and control group (G7)  with placebo  will be randomly allocated among equal size of children with autism across groups. The status of ASD will be evaluated by reviewing its clinical manifestations (for all possible signs, symptoms and comorbidities) based on the American Psychiatric Association’s Diagnostic and Statistical Manual (DSM-5). Clinical manifestations of ASD will be reviewed at different time intervals (at baseline, post 3,6 and 9 months of interventions) among all groups. The severity of ASD will be stratified and the scores of ASD are provided as (score 0: if no any manifestations occurred; score 1: mild; score 2: moderate and score 3: severe manifestation/s). Finally, the scores of ASD will be summated based on the number of presented manifestations at different time intervals and the mean score of ASD will be compared. The essential nutrient with lowest mean scores of ASD will be considered as the effective and efficient nutritional supplement in the prognosis of the disease in addition with its availability, feasibility and less cost. Data will be collected by structured questionnaire via face to face interview, physical examination and laboratory investigations. The data will be entered in to Epi-data and finally exported to SPSS for analysis. ANOVA will be applied to determine the roles of supplementation of essential nutrients in the prognosis of ASD and to sort the effective and efficient nutrients in improving its manifestations. A p-value of <0.05 will be declared as statistically significant. Based on the findings, conclusion will be drawn and recommendations will be forwarded. A total of 614,000.00 Ethiopian birr is required to accomplish the study.',NULL,'The roles of supplementation of essential nutrients in improving manifestations of autism spectrum disorders among children with autism at Ethiopian autism centers; A randomized experimental study design','2021-11-19 12:11:31','Research project team\r\nThe project involves multidisciplinary professionals where their active participation warranted accomplishing the project as per the intended objectives.','7ca7f272be1ea5e2da35a195479b850b','completed','Background and Rationale\r\nAutism is a neurodevelopmental disorder characterized by impaired social interaction, restricted interests, compromised communication skills, repetitive patterns of behavior and unusual stereotyped interests[1,2]. It is a complex, serious, biologically based disorder that first described in 1943by Leo Kanner as a triad of impairments, including social and communication difficulties and restricted interests/repetitive behaviour[3]. It has a variety of characteristic features like hyperactivity and quick frustration to any situations, social deficits, abnormalities in communication, cognitive inflexibility, irritability, aggression, self-injury, lack of attention, and several fits of bad temper where its signs and symptoms vary from mild to profound mental retardation that coined by ‘Autism Spectrum Disorder’ (ASD)[4]. People with ASD show diverse medical and behavioural problems, with multiple co morbidities (GIT dysfunction, metabolic defects, allergy, epilepsy, emotion dysregulation, sleep impairment, cardiac and respiratory problems)[5–18].\r\nThe prevalence rate of ASD is steadily rising globally per year. Autism rates in the United States are increasing at a rate of 14% to 20% per year. The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) estimates that 1 in 59 children in the U.S has autism in 2020 (1 in 75 in 2010;1 in 110 in 2009; 1 in 150 children in 2007) (with an 18% increase per year) and it is prevalence was increased by 18.9% per year in average from 2003 to 2008.The prevalence of ASD is estimated to be about 14.7 per 1000 (1 in 68) among children aged 6 years. Overall ASD prevalence varies anywhere from 5.7 to 21.9 per 1000 children aged 8 years. This significant and alarmingly rising prevalence of ASD over the last 20 years is probably not the result of better diagnosis because the same diagnostic techniques have been used since 1994[19–21].\r\nThere is no specific biochemical indicator or distinct neuroanatomical abnormality that defines autism, and the diagnosis is based on clinical and behavioral assessment after 12-14 months, but is frequently undiagnosed until age 3 when they are found to lack language and/or social skills and fail to progress. The recognized justifications for the rising of ASD rate are parallel with increasement of the incidence of obesity in young women as maternal obesity may increase the risk of neurodevelopmental disorders including ASD in children. The other possible reason is globalization effect of diffused industrial revolution that exposes parents to different chemicals and other occupation related factors[22–24].\r\nAlthough there is scarcity of literatures in Africa to date due to different barriers such as lack of diagnostic facilities, there is no reason to believe that rates of autism will be any less low elsewhere[25,26]. In Ethiopia more than 600,000 children were estimated to live with ASD. The services provided to the victims are also challenges due to limited infrastructure, human and material resources[27,28].\r\nThe impact of ASD is not limited to the affected children but, the hampered quality of life of children leads to social, psychological and spiritual impacts of families as the child with AD is discriminated/stereotyped, hidden at home with wrong spiritual beliefs. The disease also causes significant medical expenses and majority of   couples with autistic children end their marriages in divorce[29].\r\nThe cause of ASD is multi-factorial with genetic and environmental factors. Genetic factors are due to gene mutations, gene deletions, copy number variants and other genetic anomalies. Being males also increases the risks of ASD about 3-4 times fold. The identified environmental factors for the development of ASD are nutritional status of the child (feeding practices); infections; parents/caregivers socioeconomic factors; maternal obstetric history (parity, gravid, child spacing, breast feeding, ANC follow up, vaccination/ supplementation, mode of delivery, exposure to sun light); drug utilization; exposure to infections; nutritional status, behavioral factors/substance use; exercise status during prenatal, perinatal and postnatal periods; parental exposure to toxic chemicals (mercury, dioxin, chlorpyrifos, thimerosol, organophosphate, pesticides, insecticides, thalidomide, misoprostol, phthalates, valproic acid, volatile organic compounds like methylene chloride, trichloroethylene and styrene[30,31].\r\nCurrently studies were anticipated to extrapolate the roles of essential nutrients on the development and prognosis of ASD. For instance, studies revealed that optimal human breast milk feeding (early initiation of breast feeding within 1 hour of delivery, exclusive breast feeding for six months and feeding for long duration) is associated with decreased risk of ASD due to the presence of adequate nutrients (essential fatty acids, insulin-like grow factor, immune factors, oxytocin, melatonin) in breast milk with numerous health benefits for physical and neurologic development, and protecting from infections, and better cognitive functions[32–35]. Breast milk also contributes to the development of the gut microbiome where its alterations play a role in the etiology of neurodevelopmental disorders, including ASD[36–40]. Studies also revealed the advantage of exclusive breast feeding in delaying next pregnancy (child birth spacing) with less risks of ASD in the younger sibling[41–43]. \r\nThe finding of randomized controlled trials, case control studies, cohort study,meta-analysis and systematic review illustrated that improvements of cognitive status and communication skills of children with ASD after supplementation of oral vitamin D[44–48], vitamin B(B1,2,3,6,12)[49–61], folic acid [62,63], vitamin A [64,65], trace minerals (zink and iron)[66–71], oligopeptides[72] and essential fatty acids (omega -3, PUFA, arachnoid acids)[73–81], and the implementation was encouraged by women, infants, and children (WIC) program.\r\nBut, up to date no any literatures that compare the effects of multiple essential nutrients supplementation on similar population than separately reporting their advantages in comparison to control group. Thus, the current mega project will be intended to investigate the roles of essential nutrients supplementation in the prognosis of ASD among children with autism at Ethiopian Autism centers. The study also aims to sort specific effective and efficient essential nutrients supplementation to confront this significant, alarming public health problem that serve as insights for preventive and therapeutic management.','Methods\r\nThe study will be conducted at two Ethiopian autism centers (Nehemiah Autism Center and Nia foundation Joy Autism Center) both located in the capital of the country, Addis Ababa. \r\nNehemiah Autism Center (NAC) is a non-profitable organization that was founded June 16th, 2011, licensed by charities and societies agency. It has different stakeholders (director, co-director, administration, teachers, students, and the families to the students). The Center provides education and support for children with ASD and their families free of charge. The goal of NAC is to create an environment for children affected by Autism where they can enjoy their basic rights and privileges and develop to their full potential.\r\nJoy Center for Autism in Ethiopia plans to expand its current programs and build a Center of excellence that will serve 500 children with Autism and related developmental disorders in different branches throughout Ethiopia. The center will be an ideal facility to create access for the rehabilitation, educational and therapeutic services for children with autism in Ethiopia.\r\nA randomized experimental study design will be applied to assess the roles of essential nutrients supplementation in the prognosis of ASD among children with autism at Ethiopian Autism centers. Different groups of essential nutrients supplementation as intervention groups (G1-G6) and control group (G7) with placebo will be randomly allocated among equal size of children with autism across groups by administrating them with optimal dose as the standards.\r\nG1: Vitamin D3 (400IU/day PO for 9 months)\r\nG2: Omega-3 (750mg/day PO for 9 months)\r\nG3: Docosa hexanooic acid/ DHA (5g/day for 9 months)\r\nG4: Vitamin B12 (500 µg per day PO for 9 months)\r\nG5: Folic acid (400 µg per day PO for 9 months)\r\nG6: Vitamin A (1000IU/day PO for 9 months)\r\nG7: Placebo (distilled water PO for 9 months)\r\nThe status of ASD will be evaluated by reviewing its clinical manifestations (for all possible signs, symptoms and comorbidities) based on the American Psychiatric Association’s Diagnostic and Statistical Manual (DSM-5)[82]. Clinical manifestations of ASD will be reviewed for all possible signs, symptoms and comorbidities at different time intervals (at baseline, post 3,6 and 9 months of interventions) among all groups. The possible comorbidities among children with ASD will also be diagnosed by history, physical examination and laboratory investigations as the standards. The severity of ASD will be stratified and the scores of ASD are provided as (score 0: if no any manifestations occurred; score 1: mild; score 2: moderate and score 3: severe manifestation/s). Finally, the scores of ASD will be summated based on the number of presented manifestations at different time intervals and the mean score of ASD will be compared. The essential nutrient with lowest mean scores of ASD will be considered as the effective and efficient nutritional supplement in the prognosis of the disease in addition with its availability, feasibility and less cost.\r\nData will be collected both by structured questionnaire by face to face interview physical examination and laboratory investigations. The collected data will be coded and entered in to Epidata version 4.3.1 and finally exported to SPSS version 25 for further analysis. Descriptive statistical analysis will be applied to express the finding. ANOVA will be applied to determine the roles of supplementation of essential nutrients in the prognosis of ASD and to sort the effective and efficient nutritional supplementation in improving manifestations of ASD. A p-value of <0.05 will be declared as statistically significant. Finally the finding of the study will be reported by using tables, figures and narrations.','<h1><span style=\"font-size:14pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"color:#365f91\"><a name=\"_Toc88167498\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">References</span></a></span></span></span></h1>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[1]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Carey B. New definition of autism will exclude many, study suggests. New York Times 2012;20.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[2]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ousley O, Cermak T. Autism spectrum disorder: defining dimensions and subgroups. Curr