></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[16]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Tuchman R, Alessandri M, Cuccaro M. Autism spectrum disorders and epilepsy: moving towards a comprehensive approach to treatment. Brain and Development 2010;32:719&ndash;30.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[17]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Brooks-Kayal A. Epilepsy and autism spectrum disorders: are there common developmental mechanisms? Brain and Development 2010;32:731&ndash;8.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[18]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Richdale AL, Schreck KA. Sleep problems in autism spectrum disorders: prevalence, nature, &amp; possible biopsychosocial aetiologies. Sleep Medicine Reviews 2009;13:403&ndash;11.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[19]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Knopf A. Autism prevalence increases from 1 in 60 to 1 in 54: CDC. The Brown University Child and Adolescent Behavior Letter 2020;36:4&ndash;4.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[20]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Leigh JP, Du J. Brief report: Forecasting the economic burden of autism in 2015 and 2025 in the United States. Journal of Autism and Developmental Disorders 2015;45:4135&ndash;9.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[21]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Currenti SA. Understanding and determining the etiology of autism. Cellular and Molecular Neurobiology 2010;30:161&ndash;71.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[22]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hansen SN, Schendel DE, Parner ET. Explaining the increase in the prevalence of autism spectrum disorders: the proportion attributable to changes in reporting practices. JAMA Pediatrics 2015;169:56&ndash;62.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[23]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Matson JL, Kozlowski AM. The increasing prevalence of autism spectrum disorders. Research in Autism Spectrum Disorders 2011;5:418&ndash;25.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[24]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Charman T. The prevalence of autism spectrum disorders. European Child &amp; Adolescent Psychiatry 2002;11:249&ndash;56.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[25]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bakare MO, Munir KM. Autism spectrum disorders (ASD) in Africa: a perspective. African Journal of Psychiatry 2011;14:208&ndash;10.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[26]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Abubakar A, Ssewanyana D, Newton CR. A systematic review of research on autism spectrum disorders in Sub-Saharan Africa. Behavioural Neurology 2016;2016.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[27]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ethiopia: educating everyone about autism - The Lancet Neurology n.d. https://www.thelancet.com/journals/laneur/article/PIIS1474-4422(16)30297-6/fulltext (accessed July 1, 2021).</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[28]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Zeleke W. Children with Autism in Ethiopia: Diagnosis, Laws, and Educational and Behavioral Intervention. Journal of the International Association of Special Education 2016;16.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[29]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hong J, Bishop-Fitzpatrick L, Smith L, Greenberg JS, Mailick MR. Factors Associated with Subjective Quality of Life of Adults with Autism Spectrum Disorder: Self-Report vs. Maternal Reports. J Autism Dev Disord 2016;46:1368&ndash;78. https://doi.org/10.1007/s10803-015-2678-0.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[30]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Kalkbrenner AE, Schmidt RJ, Penlesky AC. Environmental Chemical Exposures and Autism Spectrum Disorders: A Review of the Epidemiological Evidence. Curr Probl Pediatr Adolesc Health Care 2014;44:277&ndash;318. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cppeds.2014.06.001.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[31]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Emberti Gialloreti L, Mazzone L, Benvenuto A, Fasano A, Garcia Alcon A, Kraneveld A, et al. Risk and Protective Environmental Factors Associated with Autism Spectrum Disorder: Evidence-Based Principles and Recommendations. J Clin Med 2019;8:217. https://doi.org/10.3390/jcm8020217.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[32]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Al-Farsi YM, Al-Sharbati MM, Waly MI, Al-Farsi OA, Al-Shafaee MA, Al-Khaduri MM, et al. Effect of suboptimal breast-feeding on occurrence of autism: A case&ndash;control study. Nutrition 2012;28:e27&ndash;32.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[33]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bar 