s New Roman&quot;,serif\">Budget breakdown</span></span></a></span></span></h1>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">A total of </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">3</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">20,000.00 Ethiopian birr is required to accomplish the study.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Table2: Budget breakdown to assess the prevalence of relaparotomy and its associated factors, and patient outcome among patients undergo laparotomy surgery at Jimma University Medical Center from February to September, 2022. Jimma, Ethiopia</span></span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border:none; width:99.96%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top; width:12%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">S.N</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top; width:52%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Category</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:1px solid black; vertical-align:top; width:34%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Total cost (in ETB)</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:12%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">1.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:52%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Stationery cost</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:34%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">10,000.00</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:12%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">3.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:52%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Personnel cost</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:34%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">3</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">10,000.00</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:12%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:52%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Total cost</span></span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n			<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:34%\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">3</span></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">20,000.00</span></span></strong></span></span></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(55,62,9,15,'The existing papar-based research project management of Jimma University has many limitations. It\'s not easy to get uptodate information on the progress of each project and aggregate data on a university wide. An online research management system with a database can solve the problems of this paper-based system. The major objective of this research project is to assess the existing work process from proposal submission till monitoring and evaluation. An online research management system will be designed and developed following an agile research methodology. Successful deployment of the system will alleviate a number of problems of the existing system.',NULL,'Design and Development of Online Proposal Submission and Research Management System','2021-11-19 12:00:44','Process indicator	Outcome indicator	Impact indicator\r\n•	Adoption of the system institute wide.\r\n•	Users /researchers feedback for using the system and 	•	Reduction of burden of colleges regarding to proposal collection and editorial management\r\n•	Report management facilitate efficiency for submission and publication of terminal report	•	Reduction of work load , paper work and timelines for editors and researchers.','38cff0fc11b78e7cad4a03b49521b21e','completed','The directorate of research publication office receives and publishes annual and special grant research as their concern. In the existing system, the processing of research submission is in two ways namely online via email and in hard copy. Every research management scenario is being  processed via email and on hard copy. No platform has been attempted to be employed or implemented to make automated the research management processes. The overall existing system workflow  is  discussed in the proposal document. The research publication workflow starts from call for proposal to the publication of the research and the invitation will be announced once a year (If the research type is University research, else if it is external grant, it has no schedule at all) and each colleges allowed to announce call for proposals so as to make researcher top up with their proposal submission.\r\nResearch being published through the research publication office are of the different categories: namely: Mega researches, CSB (Community Service Based) research, TT (Technology Transfer) research, Grant Research (external) , Conferences , Student research (MSc and PhD), Female granted research. Mega Researches are conducted by the staff members initiated annually and the budgets will be allocated as per the academic rank of the researchers. The authors or researchers will allow only one mega research at a time and are not allowed for simultaneous membership unless the researcher delivers his research in his hand.  \r\nThe very first stage of the research publication workflow starts from a call for proposal announcement. The researcher /members of each college will be allowed to apply and send their proposals to be reviewed by the editorial board. The editorial board assesses and makes a decision with regard to their guidelines and if the proposal meets minimum requirements, it proceeds; otherwise it will be declined (List of the editorial decisions of proposal submission will be mentioned later). The reviewers will be assigned to each of the proposals if the submission fits the guidelines. The review process will be completely double-blind in which the researcher and the reviewers will never know one another. Applicants of grant research could be a member of JU or could not be.\r\nGrant research proposals will be sent as researchers win the grant from another organization and will submit their approval attached with their proposal. Like most of the research submission platforms across the world, RMS will have the same process of proposal submission and publication. \r\nEach work unit will announce their annual University research proposal calls so as to allow researchers top up with their research proposal submission. The system shall allow the link that the researchers respond to the call and submit their proposal. Each college research coordinator/ principal editor or manager will assign a reviewer for each proposal. The reviewers will be invited to revise the proposal according to their interest and or their academic profile. The proposals will be assessed and reviewed by reviewers to have an editorial decision. The editorial process will be double blind in which both parts (author and reviewer) will never know one another. The budget will be allocated/ approved to the submission whose proposal fits the minimum requirement of the criteria of the guidelines and depends on the editorial decision. \r\nAt the mean time of the project workflow, the progress report will be sent to the office and the director will decide whether the submission shall proceed or not. Then if the research project shall be proceeds then all necessary proposal components shall be uploaded after the progress report approved. The final terminal report will be uploaded and sent with the data set used and the variables in the data sets. If the data sets uploaded are not real data then the director may reject them and the system shall allow researchers to re-upload them in a given time. \r\nList of all published researches will be announced to all of the applicants of the call. And the report will show the summary.','Materials and Methods\r\n3.1	Requiremnt gathering\r\nUser requirement gathering is the preliminary step in software evaluation. In this system we need to gather requirements of the potential user and domain experts .  \r\n3.2	Requirement Analysis\r\nWe use object oriented analysis (OOA) [1] methods to model the function of the system (use case modeling), find and identify the objects, organize the objects, identify the relationship between them and finally model the behavior of these objects.\r\n3.3	Modeling tools and techniques\r\nThe preferred design methodology for RMS system is hybrid of Agile [2], [3] and Waterfall system design methodology. Waterfall methodology is: “In the traditional waterfall methodology, first comes the analysis phase, then the design phase, followed by the implementation phase, with testing completing the process. The Agile-Waterfall Hybrid [4] is often considered a smart approach for adopting both methodologies without compromising too much, essentially utilizing the best of both worlds. The main aim of the hybrid methodology is to enable teams to define requirements and adapt to changing requirements through continuous feedback and delivery. The hybrid method retains the clarity and tracking system of waterfall method, while embracing the adaptability and flexibility of agile. The team that does each phase is different and there may be a management decision point at each phase transition. This methodology is called the waterfall methodology because each phase flows naturally into the next phase like water over a series of falls.\r\nThe overall process will be demonstrated in the UML diagrams [5].\r\n3.4	Experimental Plan\r\n•	Summary description of the proposed system:   in different local languages (at least three). \r\n•	Users of the system and the goals of the experiment: The potential users for the system are academic staff members of Jimma University and directorates for research publication\r\n•	Design of the experiment\r\n“Research Management System\'\' shall have two separate interfaces; (1) Back-end interface and (2) Front-end interface. The fronted interface is used by most of the system users whereas the back-end interface is used by users with administrative privilege. \r\nThe back-end interface is used to apply system wide settings. In the experiment, different subjects are randomly assigned to each of the design. From each subjects or stockholder list; we randomly select and assign them for testing. Then final result will be evaluated. This will give information about us to decide the final project outcome.','<h1 style=\"margin-left:24px\"><span style=\"font-size:14pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">References</span></span></h1>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:101px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">[1]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; G. Booch, R. A. Maksimchuk, M. W. Engle, B. J. Young, J. Connallen, and K. A. Houston, &ldquo;Object-oriented analysis and design with applications,&rdquo; <em>ACM SIGSOFT Softw. Eng. Notes</em>, vol. 33, no. 5, pp. 29&ndash;29, 2008.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:101px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">[2]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; P. Abrahamsson, O. Salo, J. Ronkainen, and J. Warsta, &ldquo;Agile software development methods: Review and analysis,&rdquo; <em>ArXiv Prepr. ArXiv170908439</em>, 2017.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:101px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">[3]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; J. Highsmith and A. Cockburn, &ldquo;Agile software development: The business of innovation,&rdquo; <em>Computer</em>, vol. 34, no. 9, pp. 120&ndash;127, 2001.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:101px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">[4]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; R. J. Kusters, Y. van de Leur, W. G. Rutten, and J. J. Trienekens, &ldquo;When agile meets waterfall-investigating risks and problems on the interface between agile and traditional software development in a hybrid development organization,&rdquo; in <em>International Conference on Enterprise Information Systems</em>, 2017, vol. 2, pp. 271&ndash;278.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:101px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">[5]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; H.-E. Eriksson and M. Penker, &ldquo;Business modeling with UML,&rdquo; <em>N. Y.</em>, pp. 1&ndash;12, 2000.</span></span></span></p>','The goal of this research is to design and develop an online  Research Management System for Jimma University Institute of Health.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'research database,software development,online research management system',10,'<p style=\"margin-left:2px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"color:black\">The research will take 7 months and the overall tasks that will be conducted in this research are summarized explicitly under time schedule.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:2px; text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:2px; text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"Table\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; margin-left:8px; width:637px\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border-bottom:2px solid black; border-left:2px solid black; border-right:none; border-top:2px solid black; height:18px; width:51px\">\r\n			<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New 