dolescent: using the menstrual cycle as a vital sign. Committee Opinion No.651. American College of obstetricians and gynecologists. Obstet Gynecol 2015;126:e143-6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></a></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Marni Sommer, 2013 Global Health Matters</span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">MenarcHe: a Missing indicator in population health from low-income countries Public Health Reports / September&ndash;October 2013 / Volume 128</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">United Nations Children&rsquo;s Fund. (2008). sharing simple facts: Useful information about menstrual health and hygiene</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Census (2015) Bureau U.S.A </span></span><a href=\"http://www.census.gov/population/\" style=\"color:blue; text-decoration:underline\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">http://www.census.gov/population/</span></span></a><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> international/data/idb/informationGateway.php</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">House et al., 2012, Sarah House, Th&eacute;r&egrave;se Mahon and Sue Cavill Menstrual hygiene Matters A resource for improving menstrual hygiene around the world 2012</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Margaret Njeri Ngugi Jasper Edward Nyaura. Demystifying the Menstruation Process among the Kenyan Girl-Child &ldquo;A Period of Shame&rdquo;: A Socio-Cultural Perspective</span></span> <span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Volume 3 Issue 10, October 2014</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Mason L, Nyothach E, Alexander K, Odhiambo FO, Eleveld A,Vulule J, et al. We keep it secret so no one should know &lsquo;qualitative study to explore young schoolgirl&rsquo;s attitudes and experiences with menstruation in rural Western Kenya. PLoSOne 2013; 8: e79132</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Maiandra GD&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Chothe V, Khubchandani J, Seabert D, et al. Students&rsquo; perceptions and doubts about menstruation in developing countries: a case study from India. Health Promot Pract 2014; 15:319&ndash;26</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\">