 New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[68]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Lukman Y. Utero-vaginal prolapse: a rural disability of the young. East Afr Med J 1995;72:2&ndash;9.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[69]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Geiss IM, Riss PA, Hanzal E, Dungl A. A simple teaching tool for training the pelvic organ prolapse quantification system. Int Urogynecology J 2007;18:1003&ndash;1005.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[70]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Bump RC, Mattiasson A, B&oslash; K, Brubaker LP, DeLancey JO, Klarskov P, et al. The standardization of terminology of female pelvic organ prolapse and pelvic floor dysfunction. Am J Obstet Gynecol 1996;175:10&ndash;17.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[71]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Barber MD, Walters MD, Bump RC. Short forms of two condition-specific quality-of-life questionnaires for women with pelvic floor disorders (PFDI-20 and PFIQ-7). Am J Obstet Gynecol 2005;193:103&ndash;113.</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">[72]&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Goba GK, Legesse AY, Zelelow YB, Gebreselassie MA, Rogers RG, Kenton KS, et al. Reliability and validity of the Tigrigna version of the Pelvic Floor Distress Inventory&ndash;Short Form 20 (PFDI-20) and Pelvic Floor Impact Questionnaire-7 (PFIQ-7). Int Urogynecology J 2019;30:65&ndash;70.</span></span></p>','To assess the burden of POP and its associated factors among childbearing and postmenopausal age mothers dwelling in Jimma zone',NULL,NUL